🎤 Interview Explanation (Short & Perfect)

👉
“I use DFS with backtracking. I try starting from every cell that matches the first character. Then I recursively explore all 4 directions while marking cells as visited. If the path fails, I backtrack by unmarking the cell. The base case is when all characters of the word are matched.”

🔁 Counter Interview Questions
❓ Q1: Why visited array?

👉 Same cell reuse avoid karne ke liye

❓ Q2: Can we solve without visited?

👉 Yes 👇

board[r][c] = '#'; // mark
// DFS
board[r][c] = original; // restore
❓ Q3: Why backtracking needed?

👉 Ek path fail ho sakta hai → doosra try karna padega

❓ Q4: Worst-case complexity?

👉 O(N * M * 4^L)

❓ Q5: Can diagonals be used?

👉 Yes → 8 directions bana do

